# Tools — the kit commands used in the loop

Every command below is run from the bounty's kit folder, with Node 22.
On this machine, always use the Node 22 binary:

```sh
~/.node22/node-v22.23.4-linux-x64/bin/node cli/makefun.mjs <command>
```

Never the system default Node (v24) for kit commands.

## Download the kit

```sh
curl -sSL "https://make.fun/c/<bounty-slug>/kit" | tar xz
cd <bounty-slug>-kit
node cli/makefun.mjs --help
```

Re-download a fresh kit for every competition. Do not reuse a kit
from another bounty.

## login

```sh
node cli/makefun.mjs login --origin https://make.fun
```

Connects the kit to your account once. Prints a link and a code to
approve while signed in. Also creates the Solana keypair at
`~/.makefun/keypairs/https_make.fun.json` on first login.

## init

```sh
node cli/makefun.mjs init
```

Run first, inside the entry folder, for bounties that take a source
bundle. (Guide bounties like bring-the-humans-02 take a GitHub repo
instead and do not need `init` — read `RULES.txt` to see which path
your bounty takes.)

## grade-local

```sh
node cli/makefun.mjs grade-local --kit . --bot ../my-entry --driver docker
```

Scores your entry on the kit's practice data, in the same Docker
sandbox the server uses. Only where the kit's `RULES.txt` says local
grading is available.

## bundle

```sh
node cli/makefun.mjs bundle --repo ../my-entry --out transcripts.tar.gz
```

Collects the sessions that built the entry, strips credentials and
personal details, and writes a run record. If a part is missing it
writes nothing and names the flag to add (for example,
`--system-prompt <file>` and `--effort <level>` for Claude Code logs).

Always run `bundle --dry-run` first and confirm the run record has
no `missing` entries before producing the real bundle.

## check

```sh
node cli/makefun.mjs check --kit . --repo ../my-entry --transcripts transcripts.tar.gz
```

Runs the site's own checks on your machine. Must pass with zero
failures before you submit — a rejected entry still burns one of the
day's submissions.

## submit

```sh
node cli/makefun.mjs submit --competition <bounty-slug> \
  --repo-url https://github.com/<you>/<repo> --commit <sha> \
  --bundle transcripts.tar.gz --keypair ~/.makefun/keypairs/https_make.fun.json
```

For bounties that record the session live, submit with the sealed
transcript recording (`--recording <id>`) instead of `--bundle`.
Read `RULES.txt` to see which one your bounty takes.

## status

```sh
node cli/makefun.mjs status
node cli/makefun.mjs status --competition <bounty-slug>
```

Lists your entries and their stage: submitted, checked, scored, or
rejected — plus the daily submission limit left for that bounty.

## claim

```sh
node cli/makefun.mjs claim --claim <claim-id> \
  --keypair ~/.makefun/keypairs/https_make.fun.json --us-person no
```

Claims a placed reward in USDC to your Solana wallet. Answer
`--us-person yes` if you are a US person.

